# Hyperbolic space, the curved bulk Vibe Theory lives in. A regular tessellation {p, q} (q regular p-gons at every
# vertex) is spherical, flat, or hyperbolic exactly as 1/p + 1/q is more than, equal to, or less than 1/2. Clearing
# the fractions, it is hyperbolic precisely when p*q is more than 2*(p + q). The mesh sits in the hyperbolic regime,
# so the bulk has constant negative curvature and the cell count grows without bound shell by shell, which is the room
# the construction needs. These curvature facts are proof-checked by `seed test`.

# The {7, 3} tiling (three heptagons at each vertex) is hyperbolic: 7*3 = 21 is more than 2*(7 + 3) = 20.
hold seven-three-tiling-is-hyperbolic
  call is-above
    call multiply
      code 7
      code 3
    call multiply
      code 2
      call add
        code 7
        code 3

# The {3, 6} tiling (six triangles at a vertex) is exactly flat, the boundary case: 3*6 = 18 equals 2*(3 + 6) = 18.
hold three-six-tiling-is-flat
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 3
      code 6
    call multiply
      code 2
      call add
        code 3
        code 6

# The {3, 4} tiling (four triangles at a vertex, the octahedron) is spherical: 3*4 = 12 is below 2*(3 + 4) = 14.
hold three-four-tiling-is-spherical
  call is-below
    call multiply
      code 3
      code 4
    call multiply
      code 2
      call add
        code 3
        code 4
